# Repository-wide attributes (ADR-50, added before the first push).
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# `core.autocrlf` is `true` on the development machine and this repository had NO `.gitattributes`,
# so every text file's line endings depended on one global setting that is invisible from inside the
# repo. That produced the warning the first audit run printed for 39 files:
#
#     warning: in the working copy of 'shared/feature_config.json',
#              LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it
#
# A contributor on Linux/macOS with `core.autocrlf=false` would then see a diff of every line of
# every file, and the Flutter/Dart/Kotlin sources have to stay byte-stable for the gates
# (`check_ps1_encoding.py`, the Kotlin<->Dart parity suites, `mel_parity_test.py`).
#
# DELIBERATELY MINIMAL
# -------------------
# This file marks **binaries** only. It contains NO `* text=auto` and NO `eol=` rule on purpose:
# either of those would renormalize every already-tracked file on the next `git add` and turn one
# commit into a whole-tree rewrite, which is exactly the churn this file is meant to prevent. The
# line-ending question for *text* files is therefore left exactly as it was -- the honest way to
# fix it is a dedicated, reviewable renormalization commit, not a side effect of a tidy-up.
#
# ADR-51 (the restructuring that made the repository root the AcouDiet project itself) added no
# path rules here, so this file survived that move unchanged: `git mv`-style moves preserve blob
# content, and the rules below match by extension, not by directory.

# ---- Rendered / captured media -----------------------------------------------------------
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# ---- Audio (the project's own noise corpus is committed; it must never be re-encoded) -----
*.wav  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.flac binary
*.ogg  binary

# ---- Model artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# `*.tflite` IS committed on purpose (4 MB, the shipped model, makes a rebuild reproducible).
*.tflite      binary
*.gguf        binary
*.safetensors binary

# ---- Archives / packages -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.zip binary
*.docx binary
*.jar binary

# ---- Delivery artifacts (gitignored; marked here so a forced add cannot corrupt them) -----
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
